{0 veins}

Database connection pooling and schema migrations for OCaml 5, on Lwt and
{{:https://github.com/paurkedal/ocaml-caqti}Caqti}, for MariaDB and PostgreSQL.

- {b Connection pools}: label-based pools for several databases, reconnecting
  after a lost connection.
- {b Roles}: statements checked against typed roles at compile time, each
  role connecting as its own database user, or {!Veins.Plain} pools without
  roles for applications with one database user.
- {b Migrations}: ordered up/down steps tracked one by one, with a global
  registry and drift detection ({!Veins.Migration}).
- {b veins-gen}: a command line tool writing migration file boilerplate.

{1 Installation}

{v
opam install veins caqti-driver-mariadb      # MariaDB / MySQL
opam install veins caqti-driver-postgresql   # PostgreSQL
v}

The opam package [veins] installs the driver libraries when their Caqti driver
is installed: depend on both in your opam file and name the library in dune,
e.g. [(libraries veins veins.mariadb)].

{1 Libraries}

{!modules: Veins Veins_mariadb Veins_postgresql}

Start with {!Veins}: its overview has a quick start, and its modules are
grouped by what an application does with them. The driver libraries give the
pool functors with the driver filled in ({!Veins_mariadb.Pools},
{!Veins_postgresql.Pools}).

The {{:https://github.com/uzh/veins#readme}README} walks through pools,
roles, logins, transactions and migrations with examples.
